  "originalTitle": "Without Prejudice",
  "overview": "Disowned by his parents at 19 after coming out, Harvey Brownstone refuses to let rejection or systemic bias define his future. Fighting his way through law school and the legal ranks, he shatters barriers to become Canada’s first openly gay judge in Ontario’s family court. Balancing a groundbreaking career on the bench with his personal search for acceptance, Harvey champions compassion and equality at every turn. Later in life, he steps down from the courtroom to reinvent himself once again as a bestselling author and television talk show host, proving that living authentically is the ultimate triumph.",
